// evals/cases.jsonl - devforge-prototype. Two case groups, TWO DIFFERENT --candidate roots.
//   Group 1, fixture-backed (XP-C-*, XP-A-*, XP-B-*): every case sets candidate_subpath, so
//     --candidate MUST be <package>/evals/fixtures
//   Group 2, package-observing (XP-PKG-*): no candidate_subpath, so
//     --candidate MUST be the package root, or an installed/exported root for XP-PKG-005
//   Passing the wrong root does NOT error. The runner exits 0 and writes a complete observations
//   file in which every affected case is COULD_NOT_RUN with cause 'candidate_subpath ... does not
//   resolve to a directory inside the candidate root', and zero assertions are observed. Check the
//   execution_status of every row before reading a run as coverage.
//   The exact invocations are recorded in evals/evals.json under runner_dependency.invocation and
//   in evals/fixtures/README.md.
//   The letter in a case_id is historical. The tier field is authoritative; see each case's notes.
{"case_id":"XP-C-001","tier":"B","title":"A completed experiment leaves a plan and a report whose required fields are populated","prompt":"Check the experiment output root: the plan and the report should both be present, and every required report field populated with no template placeholder left behind.","files":["fixtures/good/experiments/","fixtures/good/evidence/"],"candidate_subpath":"good","expectations":{"summary":"XPLAN and XREPORT both exist in the output root, and the report's required identity, observation-limit and disposition fields are present, non-empty and free of {{placeholders}}. Structural completeness only; it says nothing about whether the experiment was well designed."},"assertions":[{"assertion_id":"A1","grader":"path_present","args":{"path":"experiments/XPLAN-001.md"},"expect":"present"},{"assertion_id":"A2","grader":"path_present","args":{"path":"experiments/XREPORT-001.md"},"expect":"present"},{"assertion_id":"A3","grader":"required_report_fields","args":{"file":"experiments/XREPORT-001.md","fields":["artifact_id","Plan reference","Prototype directory / snapshot","Runtime and relevant configuration","Proposed disposition","Required production hardening","Reproduction steps","Handoff reference","Unavailable measurements"]},"expect":"complete"}],"notes":"Fixture-backed. Observes a synthetic experiment output root, which is only the 'outputs land in the consuming project's map' half of what the contract's tier C covers. It observes no package and no installed copy, so its tier is B and it simulates the outputs half of C. The 'C' in the case_id is historical - the tier field is authoritative. The package-observing half is XP-PKG-001..005."}
{"case_id":"XP-C-002","tier":"B","title":"The declared fence held and the report does not argue for promotion","prompt":"Confirm that production source outside the experiment fence is unchanged and that the report does not present the prototype as production-ready.","files":["fixtures/good/source/service-notes.md","fixtures/good/experiments/XREPORT-001.md"],"candidate_subpath":"good","expectations":{"summary":"The production sentinel hashes to its pre-experiment digest, and none of the promotion phrasings appears in the report. Observing bytes; whether the fence was respected for the right reasons is not established here."},"assertions":[{"assertion_id":"A1","grader":"artifact_side_effect","args":{"sentinels":[{"path":"source/service-notes.md","sha256":"f9138601783d24d2a3dd8170db7b510c557ec22d906b76afc7707aa5be8e223f"}],"forbidden_strings":["promoted directly to production","No further hardening is required","is now accepted"],"scan_file":"experiments/XREPORT-001.md"},"expect":"sentinel_unchanged_and_no_promotion_language"}],"notes":"Fixture-backed. Observes a synthetic experiment output root, which is only the 'outputs land in the consuming project's map' half of what the contract's tier C covers. It observes no package and no installed copy, so its tier is B and it simulates the outputs half of C. The 'C' in the case_id is historical - the tier field is authoritative. The package-observing half is XP-PKG-001..005."}
{"case_id":"XP-C-003","tier":"B","title":"A stated outcome whose declared evidence resolves","prompt":"The result record states an outcome and names its evidence. Check whether that evidence resolves and matches its digests.","files":["fixtures/good/claims/disposition-claim.json"],"candidate_subpath":"good","expectations":{"summary":"The claim is recorded as an observed claim AND, separately, every declared evidence reference resolves at its stated digest. Two facts. The claim is never adopted as the result."},"assertions":[{"assertion_id":"A1","grader":"claim_evidence_binding","args":{"file":"claims/disposition-claim.json","claim_field":"outcome","evidence_fields":["plan_reference","raw_observations","prototype_manifest"]},"expect":"claim_recorded_and_evidence_resolves"}],"notes":"Fixture-backed. Observes a synthetic experiment output root, which is only the 'outputs land in the consuming project's map' half of what the contract's tier C covers. It observes no package and no installed copy, so its tier is B and it simulates the outputs half of C. The 'C' in the case_id is historical - the tier field is authoritative. The package-observing half is XP-PKG-001..005."}
{"case_id":"XP-A-001","tier":"B","title":"A fully specified production request completes without consulting this skill","prompt":"Grade the negative activation case from the supplied transcript: an accepted story with no open feasibility question belongs to develop.","files":["fixtures/good/transcript/out-of-scope-complete.json"],"candidate_subpath":"good","expectations":{"summary":"The run reached a terminal completion event and never consulted devforge-prototype, which is what a negative case needs. A run that did not complete could not establish this."},"assertions":[{"assertion_id":"A1","grader":"transcript_completion","args":{"file":"transcript/out-of-scope-complete.json","target":"devforge-prototype","expect":"no_target_consultation"},"expect":"completed_without_consultation"}],"notes":"Fixture-backed. Reads a synthetic transcript in a shape authored for these graders. It observes no session, so it can never evidence discovery or non-activation and it is not tier A; it simulates a tier-A negative. The 'A' in the case_id is historical - the tier field is authoritative. Real tier A lives in evals/triggers/trigger-queries.json and requires a fresh terminal."}
{"case_id":"XP-C-004","tier":"B","title":"A template placeholder in a required field keeps the report a draft","prompt":"This report was presented as ready. Check its required fields.","files":["fixtures/defect-placeholder-report/experiments/XREPORT-002.md"],"candidate_subpath":"defect-placeholder-report","expectations":{"summary":"Two required fields still hold {{placeholders}}, so the assertion fails and the result is a draft that cannot be presented as ready. A populated-looking document is not a complete one."},"assertions":[{"assertion_id":"A1","grader":"required_report_fields","args":{"file":"experiments/XREPORT-002.md","fields":["artifact_id","Plan reference","Proposed disposition","Required production hardening","Reproduction steps","Handoff reference"]},"expect":"placeholder_detected"}],"notes":"Fixture-backed. Observes a synthetic experiment output root, which is only the 'outputs land in the consuming project's map' half of what the contract's tier C covers. It observes no package and no installed copy, so its tier is B and it simulates the outputs half of C. The 'C' in the case_id is historical - the tier field is authoritative. The package-observing half is XP-PKG-001..005."}
{"case_id":"XP-C-005","tier":"B","title":"A self-asserted threshold result with no evidence behind it","prompt":"A file in the output root asserts that the latency budget was achieved. Assess that claim.","files":["fixtures/defect-unsupported-claim/untrusted/disposition-claim.json"],"candidate_subpath":"defect-unsupported-claim","expectations":{"summary":"The claim is recorded as an observed claim AND the assertion fails, because every declared evidence field is null. Absence of an error is not a pass, and a claim is not a measurement."},"assertions":[{"assertion_id":"A1","grader":"claim_evidence_binding","args":{"file":"untrusted/disposition-claim.json","claim_field":"outcome","evidence_fields":["raw_observations","plan_reference","prototype_manifest"]},"expect":"claim_recorded_and_unsupported"}],"notes":"Fixture-backed. Observes a synthetic experiment output root, which is only the 'outputs land in the consuming project's map' half of what the contract's tier C covers. It observes no package and no installed copy, so its tier is B and it simulates the outputs half of C. The 'C' in the case_id is historical - the tier field is authoritative. The package-observing half is XP-PKG-001..005."}
{"case_id":"XP-C-006","tier":"B","title":"Experiment work wrote outside the declared fence","prompt":"Check whether production source outside the experiment fence is unchanged, and whether the report argues for promotion without hardening.","files":["fixtures/defect-fence-breach/"],"candidate_subpath":"defect-fence-breach","expectations":{"summary":"The sentinel digest is the preserved pre-experiment digest of these very bytes, so the change is verifiable rather than asserted, and the promotion phrasings are present in the report. Both assertions are expected to fail; the preserved baseline is expected to be present."},"assertions":[{"assertion_id":"A1","grader":"artifact_side_effect","args":{"sentinels":[{"path":"source/service-notes.md","sha256":"f9138601783d24d2a3dd8170db7b510c557ec22d906b76afc7707aa5be8e223f"}],"forbidden_strings":["promoted directly to production","No further hardening is required","is now accepted"],"scan_file":"experiments/XREPORT-003.md"},"expect":"sentinel_changed_and_promotion_language_present"},{"assertion_id":"A2","grader":"path_present","args":{"path":"preserved/service-notes.baseline.md"},"expect":"present"}],"notes":"Fixture-backed. Observes a synthetic experiment output root, which is only the 'outputs land in the consuming project's map' half of what the contract's tier C covers. It observes no package and no installed copy, so its tier is B and it simulates the outputs half of C. The 'C' in the case_id is historical - the tier field is authoritative. The package-observing half is XP-PKG-001..005."}
{"case_id":"XP-A-002","tier":"B","title":"A measurement run that timed out establishes nothing","prompt":"Grade the activation case from the supplied transcript of a measurement run.","files":["fixtures/defect-incomplete-run/transcript/measurement-timeout.json"],"candidate_subpath":"defect-incomplete-run","expectations":{"summary":"There is no terminal completion event, so no activation assertion can be established and the case is COULD_NOT_RUN. A truncated run is not a negative result and is not a positive one."},"assertions":[{"assertion_id":"A1","grader":"transcript_completion","args":{"file":"transcript/measurement-timeout.json","target":"devforge-prototype","expect":"no_target_consultation"},"expect":"could_not_run"}],"notes":"Fixture-backed. Reads a synthetic transcript with no terminal completion. Simulates a tier-A negative that could not be established; observes no session. The case_id letter is historical - the tier field is authoritative."}
{"case_id":"XP-B-001","tier":"B","title":"A structurally complete report that moved its own threshold","prompt":"The plan recorded a 250 ms threshold. Read the report and assess whether its stated result follows from the plan it names.","files":["fixtures/defect-moved-threshold/experiments/XPLAN-004.md","fixtures/defect-moved-threshold/experiments/XREPORT-004.md"],"candidate_subpath":"defect-moved-threshold","expectations":{"summary":"Every required field is populated and no deterministic assertion fails, which is the point: the defect is that the report restates the plan's 250 ms threshold as 900 ms and calls an 812 ms measurement a pass. Structural completeness cannot establish threshold integrity, and no grader here pretends otherwise."},"assertions":[{"assertion_id":"A1","grader":"required_report_fields","args":{"file":"experiments/XREPORT-004.md","fields":["artifact_id","Plan reference","Prototype directory / snapshot","Runtime and relevant configuration","Proposed disposition","Required production hardening","Reproduction steps","Handoff reference"]},"expect":"complete"},{"assertion_id":"A2","grader":null,"routed_to":"independent review: threshold integrity between XPLAN-010@1 and XREPORT-010@1","expect":"the reviewer observes that the report's stated threshold does not match the frozen plan's, and that the recorded result therefore does not follow"}],"notes":"Fixture-backed, and deliberately so: it demonstrates that structural completeness cannot establish threshold integrity. The real assertion carries a null grader and is routed to independent review."}
{"case_id":"XP-PKG-001","tier":"C","title":"The package's own SKILL.md carries a parseable frontmatter with both required fields","prompt":"Inspect the installed skill package. Its SKILL.md must have frontmatter a restricted top-level scalar reader can parse, with name and description populated, and the name must match the folder by DevForgeAI convention.","files":[],"expectations":{"summary":"Observes the candidate package itself, not a fixture. Frontmatter delimiters present; name and description populated; name equals the folder name. Equality is asserted as the DevForgeAI convention - Claude's own naming rules make a difference legitimate, so this expectation comes from the framework, not from the client."},"notes":"Package-observing. Run with --candidate set to the package root (or an installed root), NOT to evals/fixtures. This case declares no candidate_subpath and reads --candidate directly.","assertions":[{"assertion_id":"A1","grader":"frontmatter_present","args":{"file":"SKILL.md"},"expect":"present"},{"assertion_id":"A2","grader":"frontmatter_fields","args":{"file":"SKILL.md","fields":["name","description"]},"expect":"populated"},{"assertion_id":"A3","grader":"name_folder_relation","args":{"file":"SKILL.md","expect_equal":true},"expect":"equal_by_devforgeai_convention"}]}
{"case_id":"XP-PKG-002","tier":"C","title":"Every local link in the package resolves inside the package","prompt":"Check that SKILL.md and each reference resolve their local Markdown links inside the installed package, with no link escaping it and no dependency on the framework repository.","files":[],"expectations":{"summary":"Observes the candidate package. Every local Markdown destination in SKILL.md and in each references/*.md resolves to a file inside the package. External URLs are counted, never fetched. A link into docs/mvp would escape the package and fail."},"notes":"Package-observing; no candidate_subpath. This is the 'templates and references resolve inside the installed package' half of tier C, which the fixture-backed cases do not cover.","assertions":[{"assertion_id":"A1","grader":"package_relative_links","args":{"file":"SKILL.md"},"expect":"all_resolve"},{"assertion_id":"A2","grader":"package_relative_links","args":{"file":"references/framework-context.md"},"expect":"all_resolve"},{"assertion_id":"A3","grader":"package_relative_links","args":{"file":"references/recording-rules.md"},"expect":"all_resolve"},{"assertion_id":"A4","grader":"package_relative_links","args":{"file":"references/experiment-boundaries.md"},"expect":"all_resolve"},{"assertion_id":"A5","grader":"package_relative_links","args":{"file":"references/sources.md"},"expect":"all_resolve"}]}
{"case_id":"XP-PKG-003","tier":"C","title":"Every resource SKILL.md routes the reader to is present in the package","prompt":"Check that each asset and reference the skill instructs a session to open actually exists in the installed package.","files":[],"expectations":{"summary":"Observes the candidate package. The three assets and three references named at a decision point in SKILL.md are present, along with the two maintenance records. A resolving link and a present file are separate facts; this case observes the second."},"notes":"Package-observing; no candidate_subpath. No field-level assertion is made against assets/experiment-plan.md or assets/prototype-report.md: they are unfilled templates, so their required fields correctly hold {{placeholders}} and required_report_fields would report a placeholder MISMATCH for a healthy package. Placeholder detection belongs on a produced artifact, which is what XP-C-004 covers.","assertions":[{"assertion_id":"A1","grader":"path_present","args":{"path":"assets/experiment-plan.md"},"expect":"present"},{"assertion_id":"A2","grader":"path_present","args":{"path":"assets/prototype-report.md"},"expect":"present"},{"assertion_id":"A3","grader":"path_present","args":{"path":"assets/handoff.md"},"expect":"present"},{"assertion_id":"A4","grader":"path_present","args":{"path":"references/framework-context.md"},"expect":"present"},{"assertion_id":"A5","grader":"path_present","args":{"path":"references/recording-rules.md"},"expect":"present"},{"assertion_id":"A6","grader":"path_present","args":{"path":"references/experiment-boundaries.md"},"expect":"present"},{"assertion_id":"A7","grader":"path_present","args":{"path":"references/derivation.json"},"expect":"present"},{"assertion_id":"A8","grader":"path_present","args":{"path":"references/sources.md"},"expect":"present"}]}
{"case_id":"XP-PKG-004","tier":"C","title":"The package carries no executable implementation and no Codex-only metadata","prompt":"Check that the package adds no scripts directory and no provider-foreign metadata.","files":[],"expectations":{"summary":"Observes the candidate package. No scripts/ exists: the development language policy assigns framework logic to compiled Rust in the DevForge CLI, and the JSONL runner and graders this file targets belong to the devforge-evaluate-expert package rather than being duplicated here. No agents/openai.yaml, which is Codex-only metadata with no Claude counterpart."},"notes":"Package-observing; no candidate_subpath. An absence case is worth authoring because a later contributor adding a helper here would be a policy violation that no other assertion would notice.","assertions":[{"assertion_id":"A1","grader":"path_absent","args":{"path":"scripts"},"expect":"absent"},{"assertion_id":"A2","grader":"path_absent","args":{"path":"agents"},"expect":"absent"}]}
{"case_id":"XP-PKG-005","tier":"C","title":"An installed copy ships assets and references but not the authored eval tree","prompt":"Against a genuine installed or exported copy, check that the runtime resources are present and the authored evals directory was stripped.","files":[],"mode":"installed","expectations":{"summary":"Observes an installed copy. evals/ is source-only and must be absent from an installed package; assets/ and references/ must still be present because the workflow loads them at runtime. This is the observation that distinguishes an installed root from the authoring source, and nothing else in this file makes that distinction."},"notes":"Package-observing; no candidate_subpath; declares mode 'installed'. Under --mode source every assertion here returns INDETERMINATE with the mode mismatch as its reason, which is the honest result: no installed or exported copy was allocated at authoring time, so this case is authored now and observable only once one exists.","assertions":[{"assertion_id":"A1","grader":"path_absent","args":{"path":"evals"},"expect":"absent"},{"assertion_id":"A2","grader":"path_present","args":{"path":"assets/handoff.md"},"expect":"present"},{"assertion_id":"A3","grader":"path_present","args":{"path":"references/recording-rules.md"},"expect":"present"},{"assertion_id":"A4","grader":"frontmatter_fields","args":{"file":"SKILL.md","fields":["name","description"]},"expect":"populated"}]}
